            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0695" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg607"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newberry to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 585.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you that Bartlett has
                    evidently left Kara Hissar. A telegram I sent him on Saturday has been returned
                    here with the information that Bartlett has left that place. A short letter to
                        <pb facs="0696" n="608" xml:id="pg608"/> Dr. Dwight, dated the 18th, says
                    the authorities have finally moved, and have arrested the ringleader in the
                    attack on his house and sent, him to Constantinople. The petty insults and
                    persecutions, however, towards the converts of the mission still keep up, and I
                    can see no way to offer them protection.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. R. Newberry</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
